  "representation": {
    "installation": "Primary and child ArrayBuffer realms use the same installer for constructors, own prototype methods, accessors, species and tag. ArrayBuffer and SharedArrayBuffer share the species/tag installation operation.",
    "properties": "Backing state remains in ArrayBuffer cells. Installed accessors expose it through ordinary descriptor/prototype lookup; removed the virtual-property reader, duplicate byteLength branch and obsolete cache bypass. Prototype deletion, replacement, overriding getters and own shadowing are observed.",
    "identity": "Species getters share implementation but each constructor owns a distinct native function object, as required by observable identity. The existing realm-native factory binds each getter to its constructor realm.",
    "reduction": "Removed partial child ArrayBuffer installation, redundant getter-list branch, virtual-property projection and one cache guard. No new side maps, suite input changes, production JS shims or duplicate unit tests."
  },
